      "step": 14,
      "user_message": "What did we decide on for my new plant to grow at home? Can you please help me recall?",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should recall from memory: Plant Name",
      "agent_response": "You decided on a snake plant (Dracaena trifasciata) for your new home plant.\n\nQuick reminders for a beginner:\n- Light: tolerates low to bright indirect light (avoids direct harsh sun).  \n- Water: infrequent — let soil mostly dry between waterings (roughly every 2–6 weeks depending on light/season). Avoid overwatering.  \n- Soil & pot: well-draining potting mix and a pot with drainage holes.  \n- Temp & humidity: comfortable at normal indoor temps (60–85°F / 16–29°C); average home humidity is fine.  \n- Care: minimal — occasional light feeding in spring/summer; wipe leaves if dusty.\n\nWant a simple watering schedule or a reminder plan I can set up (weekly/biweekly)?",
      "duration_s": 14.78,
      "passed": true,
      "success_check": {
        "type": "cross_step_semantic_judge",
        "reference_step": 1,
        "extract_focus": "Plant Name",
        "comparison_query": "The agent must correctly state the specific Plant Name from the previous conversation. If the agent explicitly states it doesn't have the information saved (e.g., 'I don't have that saved', 'I can't recall', 'I don't have that stored'), the response should FAIL even if it then suggests something similar. If the agent correctly states the information without indicating it doesn't have it saved, the response should PASS.",
        "compare_focus": "Plant Name"
      }
    },
    {
      "step": 15,
      "user_message": "Can you help me recall the school event game we decided on for my event?",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should recall from memory: \"school event game\"",
      "agent_response": "I don't see a specific school-event game saved in your memories — we noted you’re organizing a school event, but no final game choice was recorded. I can help you pick one quickly. To narrow it, what age group and venue (indoor/outdoor) are you planning for, and roughly how many participants?\n\nMeanwhile, here are proven, easy-to-run options by type (with quick notes on setup, group size, and materials):\n\n- Scavenger Hunt\n  - Best for: all ages (tailor clues)\n  - Group size: small teams\n  - Materials: clue list, small prizes\n  - Why: active, collaborative, low cost\n\n- Relay Races (sack race, spoon/egg)\n  - Best for: elementary — middle school\n  - Group size: teams of 4–10\n  - Materials: sacks/spoons/eggs or cones\n  - Why: high energy, competitive, simple rules\n\n- Minute-to-Win-It Games\n  - Best for: all ages, very flexible\n  - Group size: individuals or teams\n  - Materials: household items (cups, straws, cookies)\n  - Why: fast rounds, great for variety stations\n\n- Trivia Quiz / Quiz Bowl\n  - Best for: older kids, teens\n  - Group size: teams\n  - Materials: questions, buzzers or score sheets, projector (optional)\n  - Why: low physical setup, inclusive for varied skills\n\n- Classroom Escape Room / Puzzle Challenge\n  - Best for: older kids & teens\n  - Group size: teams of 4–8\n  - Materials: printed clues, locks (optional), props\n  - Why: excellent for critical thinking and teamwork\n\n- Human Knot / Team-Building Challenges\n  - Best for: team-building across ages (with supervision)\n  - Group size: 6–12 per group\n  - Materials: none\n  - Why: fosters communication and cooperation\n\n- Obstacle Course\n  - Best for: active groups, outdoor\n  - Group size: individuals timed or teams\n  - Materials: cones, ropes, hurdles\n  - Why: customizable difficulty, very engaging\n\n- Talent Show / Open Mic\n  - Best for: mixed ages, creative crowd\n  - Group size: any\n  - Materials: microphone, small stage area, sign-up sheet\n  - Why: showcases students’ talents; low physical demand\n\nIf you tell me age range, indoor vs outdoor, time available, and whether you want competitive or cooperative activities, I’ll recommend the best option and can draft rules, a schedule, materials checklist, and prize ideas. Which details should I use?",
      "duration_s": 20.175,
      "passed": false,
      "success_check": {
        "type": "cross_step_semantic_judge",
